% Chapter 42 of the tariff (Section VIII): articles of leather; saddlery and
% harness; travel goods, handbags and similar containers; articles of animal
% gut (other than silkworm gut) — all five headings (4201, 4202, 4203, 4205,
% 4206; 4204 is no longer used) and their 20 six-digit subheadings. A
% library: it includes chapter_64.le (and through it chapter_39.le,
% section_xi.le and gri.le) and chapter_71.le, because the notes of
% Chapters 39, 42, 64 and 71 and of Section XI send goods between these
% chapters; tariff.le includes it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 23 (2026), Chapter 42 notes 1 to 4 and Additional
% U.S. notes 1 and 2, and the terms of the headings and subheadings
% (https://hts.usitc.gov/); Section VIII has no notes. Chapter 39 note 2(m),
% Section XI note 1(l), Chapter 71 note 3(e). The subheadings are the
% six-digit HS ones. US Customs rulings name the containers and say how the
% outer surface is read; HQ H284146 quotes the Explanatory Note to heading
% 4202 on its two parts.
%
% How the chapter is read. Heading 4202 has two lists of containers,
% divided by a semicolon. The containers of the first list (trunks,
% suitcases, briefcases, spectacle cases, camera cases, holsters and similar
% containers) may be of any material. The containers of the second list
% (travelling bags, backpacks, handbags, shopping bags, wallets, purses,
% tool bags, jewelry boxes and similar containers) must be of leather or
% composition leather, of sheeting of plastics, of textile materials, of
% vulcanized fiber or of paperboard, or be covered with such materials or
% with paper (Explanatory Note, quoted in HQ H284146). The facts of a
% container are its kind (a handbag, a backpack, a wallet...) and its outer
% surface:
%   the outer surface of G is of M
%   the outer surface of G is N percent of M   (the material that covers
%       the greatest part gives the essential character, NY N252193)
% The subheadings read the group of the kind (trunks and similar
% containers; handbags; articles carried in the pocket or in the handbag;
% other) and the class of the outer surface (leather; sheeting of plastics
% or textile; other plastics; other). Additional U.S. note 2 (a textile
% coated with plastics is read by its exterior surface) is the reader's
% judgment when the fact is written (NY N297423).
% Heading 4201 takes saddlery and harness for any animal, of any material.
% Heading 4203 takes articles of apparel and clothing accessories of leather
% or of composition leather (note 4: gloves, belts, braces); heading 4205
% other articles of leather; heading 4206 articles of gut, goldbeater's
% skin, bladders or tendons. A good is of leather when what it is
% classified as consisting of is wholly or mainly of leather (GRI 3(b): the
% leather that girds the waist gives a belt its essential character, NY
% N291699).
% Note 2 excludes footwear (Chapter 64), imitation jewelry (7117) and
% netting (5608), written below; the other goods of note 2 (catgut of 3006,
% articles lined with fur, headgear, whips, harness fittings, musical
% instruments, furniture, toys, buttons) are outside the model: a claim that
% a good belongs there is answered by the office (gri.le).
%
% A protective phone case that holds only the device and leaves it fully
% working is not a container of heading 4202 (HQ H284146, following the
% court in Otter Products): it is an article of its material (3926 for
% plastics). A phone case that also holds cards is a container of the
% first list.
%
% Not modelled: the lines below six digits; whether a container is of the
% second list when its outer surface is of no listed material but is
% covered with paper (the reader writes "paper" as its outer surface).
%
% Provenance: every rule and table is labelled and cites the passage it
% encodes; the documents say where their text is (sources/), so the editor
% shows each passage and the verifier checks every quotation.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the tariff or of the rulings it
% cites, it is not a binding classification ruling, and it is not legal or
% customs advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them for a real
% import, export or declaration; consult the official texts, the customs
% authority and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no liability for
% any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a family* is a family of chapter forty-two goods.
    *a family* is a family of the first part of heading 4202.
    *a family* is a family of the second part of heading 4202.
    *a family* is a family of the group *a group*.
    the outer surface of *a good* is of *a material*; undefined.
    the outer surface of *a good* is *a number* percent of *a material*; undefined.
    the outer surface material of *a good* is *a material*.
    *a material* is of the outer surface class *a class*.
    the outer surface class of *a good* is *a class*.
    *a material* is a material of the second part of heading 4202.
    *a good* is not designed for prolonged use; undefined.
    *a good* is a made up article of netting; undefined.
    *a good* is specially designed for use in sports; undefined.
    *a good* is a sterile surgical suture material; undefined.
    *a good* is of leather or of composition leather.
    *a material* is a material of heading 4206.
    *a good* has parts of chapter seventy-one that give its essential character.
    the container group of *a good* is *a group*.
    the leather article group of *a good* is *a group*.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for *a group* with surface *a class* is *a code* under table containers.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for the leather article *a group* is *a code* under table leather articles.

