% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: the goods of the chapter's families. Articles of
% leather, of gut or of plastics are manufactured articles (chapter_39.le);
% garments and clothing accessories of leather are garments (section_xi.le).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the model covers the saddlery, containers and belts of Chapter 42
rule leather_scope_family:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter forty-two goods.

saddlery is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Saddlery and harness for any animal".
luggage is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Trunks, suitcases, vanity cases, attache cases, briefcases, school satchels and similar containers".
case is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "spectacle cases, binocular cases, camera cases, musical instrument cases, gun cases, holsters and similar containers".
pocket case is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of a kind normally carried in the pocket or in the handbag".
handbag is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Handbags, whether or not with shoulder strap, including those without handle".
pocket article is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of a kind normally carried in the pocket or in the handbag".
travel bag is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "the expression \"travel, sports and similar bags\" means goods".
other container is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "tool bags, sports bags, bottle cases, jewelry boxes, powder cases, cutlery cases and similar containers".
belt is a family of chapter forty-two goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Belts and bandoliers with or without buckles".

% The two parts of heading 4202, divided by the semicolon (EN 42.02, quoted
% in HQ H284146)
luggage is a family of the first part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "Subject to Notes 2 and 3 to this Chapter, the articles covered by the first part of the heading may be of any material".
case is a family of the first part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "Subject to Notes 2 and 3 to this Chapter, the articles covered by the first part of the heading may be of any material".
pocket case is a family of the first part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "Subject to Notes 2 and 3 to this Chapter, the articles covered by the first part of the heading may be of any material".
handbag is a family of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "The articles covered by the second part of the heading must, however, be only of the materials specified therein".
pocket article is a family of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "The articles covered by the second part of the heading must, however, be only of the materials specified therein".
travel bag is a family of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "The articles covered by the second part of the heading must, however, be only of the materials specified therein".
other container is a family of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "The articles covered by the second part of the heading must, however, be only of the materials specified therein".

% The groups of the subheadings
luggage is a family of the group luggage,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Trunks, suitcases, vanity cases, attache cases, briefcases, school satchels and similar containers".
handbag is a family of the group handbag,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Handbags, whether or not with shoulder strap, including those without handle".
pocket case is a family of the group pocket,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "These subheadings cover articles of a kind normally carried in the pocket or in the handbag and include spectacle cases".
pocket article is a family of the group pocket,
    as stated in ruling HQ H284146, confer "These subheadings cover articles of a kind normally carried in the pocket or in the handbag and include spectacle cases".
case is a family of the group other,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Other: 4202.99".
travel bag is a family of the group other,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "other than those falling in subheadings 4202.11 through 4202.39".
other container is a family of the group other,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Other: 4202.99".

