% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The outer surface and its class.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the outer surface material: as the ruling states it; or the material that
% covers the greatest part of the outer surface (NY N252193); or, when the
% ruling names no outer surface, the material the good is wholly or mainly
% of (the heading: "or wholly or mainly covered with such materials")
rule outer_surface_stated with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "of leather or of composition leather, of sheeting of plastics, of textile materials, of vulcanized fiber or of paperboard, or wholly or mainly covered with such materials or with paper":
the outer surface material of a good is a material
    if the outer surface of the good is of the material.

rule outer_surface_shares with provenance ruling NY N252193,
        confer "The suede covers the majority of the outer surface. As such, it is the suede that gives the wallet its essential character":
the outer surface material of a good is a material
    if the outer surface of the good is a number percent of the material
    and it is not the case that
        the outer surface of the good is of an other material
    and it is not the case that
        the outer surface of the good is an other number percent of a second material
        and the other number > the number.

rule outer_surface_body with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "of leather or of composition leather, of sheeting of plastics, of textile materials, of vulcanized fiber or of paperboard, or wholly or mainly covered with such materials or with paper":
the outer surface material of a good is a material
    if the good is wholly or mainly of the material
    and it is not the case that
        the outer surface of the good is of an other material
    and it is not the case that
        the outer surface of the good is a number percent of a second material.

rule outer_surface_class with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "With outer surface of sheeting of plastics or of textile materials":
the outer surface class of a good is a class
    if the outer surface material of the good is a material
    and the material is of the outer surface class the class.

rule outer_surface_class_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Other: 4202.99":
the outer surface class of a good is other
    if the outer surface material of the good is a material
    and it is not the case that
        the material is of the outer surface class a class.

% Note 1: leather includes chamois, patent, patent laminated and metalized
% leather; the subheadings put composition leather with leather
leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "With outer surface of leather or of composition leather".
composition leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "With outer surface of leather or of composition leather".
chamois leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "the term \"leather\" includes chamois (including combination chamois) leather, patent leather, patent laminated leather and metalized leather".
patent leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "the term \"leather\" includes chamois (including combination chamois) leather, patent leather, patent laminated leather and metalized leather".
patent laminated leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "the term \"leather\" includes chamois (including combination chamois) leather, patent leather, patent laminated leather and metalized leather".
metalized leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "the term \"leather\" includes chamois (including combination chamois) leather, patent leather, patent laminated leather and metalized leather".
suede leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in ruling NY N252193, confer "outer surface of 85% suede leather".
split leather is of the outer surface class leather,
    as stated in ruling NY N251118, confer "It is the split leather that girds the waist and provides the essential character of the belt".
% sheeting of plastics and textile materials (paper yarn is a textile
% material, NY N338202; a textile fibre of Section XI, below)
sheeting of plastics is of the outer surface class sheeting-textile,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "With outer surface of sheeting of plastics or of textile materials".
textile materials is of the outer surface class sheeting-textile,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "With outer surface of sheeting of plastics or of textile materials".
paper yarn is of the outer surface class sheeting-textile,
    as stated in ruling NY N338202, confer "This construction is considered to be a textile material for tariff purposes".
% plastics other than sheeting (a molded case): subheading 4202.12 names
% plastics, the others sheeting of plastics only
plastics is of the outer surface class plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "With outer surface of plastics or of textile materials: 4202.12".

rule outer_surface_textile_fibre with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "With outer surface of sheeting of plastics or of textile materials":
a material is of the outer surface class sheeting-textile
    if the material belongs to a group.

rule outer_surface_polymer with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "With outer surface of plastics or of textile materials: 4202.12":
a material is of the outer surface class plastics
    if the material is a polymer of a monomer
    and it is not the case that
        the material belongs to a group.

% the materials of the second part of the heading
rule second_part_material with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "of leather or of composition leather, of sheeting of plastics, of textile materials, of vulcanized fiber or of paperboard, or wholly or mainly covered with such materials or with paper":
a material is a material of the second part of heading 4202
    if the material is of the outer surface class a class
    and the class is in [leather, sheeting-textile].

vulcanized fiber is a material of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "of textile materials, of vulcanized fiber or of paperboard".
paperboard is a material of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "of textile materials, of vulcanized fiber or of paperboard".
paper is a material of the second part of heading 4202,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "or wholly or mainly covered with such materials or with paper".

% a good is of leather when what it is classified as consisting of (GRI
% 3(b)) is wholly or mainly of leather or of composition leather
rule of_leather with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Articles of apparel and clothing accessories, of leather or of composition leather":
a good is of leather or of composition leather
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is wholly or mainly of a material
    and the material is of the outer surface class leather.

gut is a material of heading 4206,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of gut (other than silkworm gut), of goldbeater's skin".
goldbeater's skin is a material of heading 4206,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of gut (other than silkworm gut), of goldbeater's skin".
bladder is a material of heading 4206,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "of bladders or of tendons".
tendon is a material of heading 4206,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "of bladders or of tendons".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1), each with the notes that take goods out of it.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule heading_4201 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Saddlery and harness for any animal (including traces, leads, knee pads, muzzles, saddle cloths, saddle bags, dog coats and the like), of any material":
a good is described by heading 4201
    if the family of the good is saddlery.

% heading 4202, first part: of any material
rule heading_4202_first with provenance ruling HQ H284146,
        confer "Subject to Notes 2 and 3 to this Chapter, the articles covered by the first part of the heading may be of any material":
a good is described by heading 4202
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of the first part of heading 4202.

% heading 4202, second part: of the materials the heading names
rule heading_4202_second with provenance ruling HQ H284146,
        confer "The articles covered by the second part of the heading must, however, be only of the materials specified therein or must be wholly or mainly covered with such materials or with paper":
a good is described by heading 4202
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of the second part of heading 4202
    and the outer surface material of the good is a material
    and the material is a material of the second part of heading 4202.

% cigarette cases and powder cases are named by the second part; Chapter 71
% names them as personal articles (its kinds cigarette case, powder box)
rule heading_4202_personal with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "wallets, purses, map cases, cigarette cases, tobacco pouches":
a good is described by heading 4202
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [cigarette case, powder box]
    and the outer surface material of the good is a material
    and the material is a material of the second part of heading 4202.

% heading 4203: apparel and clothing accessories of leather (note 4:
% gloves, aprons, braces, belts, bandoliers, wrist straps)
rule heading_4203_apparel with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Articles of apparel and clothing accessories, of leather or of composition leather":
a good is described by heading 4203
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of garments
    and the good is of leather or of composition leather.

rule heading_4203_accessory with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "the expression \"articles of apparel and clothing accessories\" applies, inter alia, to gloves, mittens and mitts (including those for sport or for protection), aprons and other protective clothing, braces, belts, bandoliers and wrist straps":
a good is described by heading 4203
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of clothing accessories
    and the good is of leather or of composition leather.

rule heading_4203_belt with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "the expression \"articles of apparel and clothing accessories\" applies, inter alia, to gloves, mittens and mitts (including those for sport or for protection), aprons and other protective clothing, braces, belts, bandoliers and wrist straps":
a good is described by heading 4203
    if the family of the good is belt
    and the good is of leather or of composition leather.

% heading 4205: other articles of leather (GRI 3(a) below prefers the
% headings that name the article)
rule heading_4205 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Other articles of leather or of composition leather":
a good is described by heading 4205
    if the good is a manufactured article
    and the good is of leather or of composition leather.

% heading 4206: articles of gut, goldbeater's skin, bladders or tendons
rule heading_4206 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Articles of gut (other than silkworm gut), of goldbeater's skin, of bladders or of tendons":
a good is described by heading 4206
    if the good is a manufactured article
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is wholly or mainly of a material
    and the material is a material of heading 4206.

% Note 2(a): sterile surgical catgut (heading 3006)
rule note_42_2a with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Sterile surgical catgut or similar sterile suture materials (heading 3006)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 4201
    and the heading <= 4206
    and the good is a sterile surgical suture material.

% Note 2(c): made up articles of netting (heading 5608)
rule note_42_2c with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Made up articles of netting (heading 5608)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 4201
    and the heading <= 4206
    and the good is a made up article of netting.

% Note 2(d): articles of Chapter 64
rule note_42_2d with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of chapter 64;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 4201
    and the heading <= 4206
    and the other heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6404, 6405, 6406]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Note 2(g): imitation jewelry of heading 7117
rule note_42_2g with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Cuff-links, bracelets or other imitation jewelry (heading 7117)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 4201
    and the heading <= 4206
    and the good is imitation jewelry.

% Note 3(A)(a): bags of sheeting of plastics with handles, not designed for
% prolonged use (heading 3923)
rule note_42_3Aa with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Bags made of sheeting of plastics, whether or not printed, with handles, not designed for prolonged use (heading 3923)":
a good is excluded from heading 4202
    if the outer surface material of the good is sheeting of plastics
    and the good is not designed for prolonged use.

% Note 3(A)(b): articles of plaiting materials (heading 4602)
rule note_42_3Ab with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of plaiting materials (heading 4602)":
a good is excluded from heading 4202
    if the outer surface material of the good is plaiting materials.

% Note 3(B): an article of 4202 or 4203 with parts of precious metal,
% pearls or stones stays in Chapter 42, unless those parts give it its
% essential character (then Chapter 71; Chapter 71 note 3(e))
rule note_42_3B with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "If, on the other hand, the parts give the articles their essential character, the articles are to be classified in chapter 71":
a good has parts of chapter seventy-one that give its essential character
    if a component is a component of the good
    and the essential character of the good is given by the component
    and the component incorporates pearls or stones.

rule note_42_3B_metal with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "If, on the other hand, the parts give the articles their essential character, the articles are to be classified in chapter 71":
a good has parts of chapter seventy-one that give its essential character
    if a component is a component of the good
    and the essential character of the good is given by the component
    and the component contains precious metal beyond minor constituents.

rule note_42_3B_out with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "If, on the other hand, the parts give the articles their essential character, the articles are to be classified in chapter 71":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [4202, 4203]
    and the good has parts of chapter seventy-one that give its essential character.

rule note_71_3e with provenance HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71,
        confer "Articles of heading 4202 or 4203 referred to in note 3(B) to chapter 42;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 7101
    and the heading <= 7118
    and the other heading is in [4202, 4203]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading
    and it is not the case that
        the good has parts of chapter seventy-one that give its essential character.

% Chapter 39 note 2(m): saddlery and harness of 4201, containers of 4202
rule note_39_2m with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "(m) Saddlery or harness (heading 4201) or trunks, suitcases, handbags or other containers of heading 4202;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3926
    and the other heading is in [4201, 4202]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Section XI note 1(l): textile articles of 4201 and 4202
rule note_xi_1l with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "(l) Articles of textile materials of heading 4201 or 4202;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 5001
    and the heading <= 6310
    and the other heading is in [4201, 4202]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% GRI 3(a): 4205 is the residual heading of the articles of leather; the
% leather apparel and accessories of 4203 are named there, not in the
% textile headings of Section XI (note 4 names braces, which heading 6212
% also names "whether or not knitted")
rule gri_3a_4205 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 4205
    if the heading is in [4201, 4202, 4203].

rule gri_3a_4203 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading 4203 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 5001
    and the heading <= 6310.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule container_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 4202 is a code
    if the container group of the good is a group
    and the outer surface class of the good is a class
    and the subheading in heading 4202 for the group with surface the class is the code under table containers.

rule container_group with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Articles of a kind normally carried in the pocket or in the handbag":
the container group of a good is a group
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of the group the group.

rule container_group_personal with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Articles of a kind normally carried in the pocket or in the handbag":
the container group of a good is pocket
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [cigarette case, powder box].

rule leather_article_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [4201, 4203, 4205, 4206]
    and the leather article group of the good is a group
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the leather article the group is the code under table leather articles.

rule group_apparel with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Articles of apparel: 4203.10":
the leather article group of a good is apparel
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of garments.

rule group_sports_gloves with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Specially designed for use in sports: 4203.21":
the leather article group of a good is sports gloves
    if the family of the good is gloves
    and the good is specially designed for use in sports.

rule group_gloves with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Gloves, mittens and mitts:":
the leather article group of a good is gloves
    if the family of the good is gloves
    and it is not the case that
        the good is specially designed for use in sports.

rule group_belt with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Belts and bandoliers with or without buckles":
the leather article group of a good is belt
    if the family of the good is belt.

rule group_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42, confer "Other clothing accessories: 4203.40":
the leather article group of a good is other
    if the good is within the scope of the model
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family
        and the family is in [gloves, belt]
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family
        and the family is a family of garments.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests: goods with the facts a reader writes from a ruling.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

% The rulings' containers (CBP: the codes the rulings give, at six digits)
scenario containers is:
    % NY N125027: handbag, outer surface of polyurethane plastic sheeting ->
    % 4202.22
    the kind of style D-0209605NW is handbag.
    the outer surface of style D-0209605NW is of sheeting of plastics.
    % NY N252193: wallet, outer surface 85 percent suede leather and 15
    % percent PU sheeting -> 4202.31; wristlet handbag of PU sheeting ->
    % 4202.22; briefcase, 55 percent suede and 45 percent PU -> 4202.11
    the kind of style 2759 is wallet.
    the outer surface of style 2759 is 85 percent of suede leather.
    the outer surface of style 2759 is 15 percent of sheeting of plastics.
    the kind of style 3022 is handbag.
    the outer surface of style 3022 is of sheeting of plastics.
    the kind of style 2869 is briefcase.
    the outer surface of style 2869 is 55 percent of suede leather.
    the outer surface of style 2869 is 45 percent of sheeting of plastics.
    % NY N065202: backpack, outer surface of 100 percent polyester -> 4202.92
    the kind of style 8763 is backpack.
    the outer surface of style 8763 is of polyester.
    % NY N338202: tote bag, outer surface of paper yarns (a textile) -> 4202.92
    the kind of style 220381001 is tote bag.
    the outer surface of style 220381001 is of paper yarn.
    % NY L82909: tote bag of cotton canvas -> 4202.92
    the kind of style 602 is tote bag.
    the outer surface of style 602 is of cotton.
    % HQ H284146: Vault phone case of molded plastics with slots for cards ->
    % 4202.39; Protector case that only holds the phone -> 3926.90
    the kind of the Vault case is phone wallet case.
    the outer surface of the Vault case is of plastics.
    the kind of the Protector case is protective phone case.
    the Protector case is a manufactured article.
    the Protector case is made of plastics.
    the principal use of the Protector case is other use,
        according to CBP, because "although the Commuter and Defender series cases protected the device, they did not organize, store, or carry".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style D-0209605NW is 4202.22", "the subheading of style 2759 is 4202.31", "the subheading of style 3022 is 4202.22", "the subheading of style 2869 is 4202.11", "the subheading of style 8763 is 4202.92", "the subheading of style 220381001 is 4202.92", "the subheading of style 602 is 4202.92", "the subheading of the Vault case is 4202.39", "the subheading of the Protector case is 3926.90"].

% Saddlery, belts and other articles of leather
scenario leather_articles is:
    % NY N303997: dog collar of man-made textile -> 4201.00 (not Section XI,
    % note 1(l))
    the kind of the textile collar is dog collar.
    the textile collar is wholly or mainly of polyester.
    % NY M83255: nylon dog leash -> 4201.00
    the kind of style 946510 is dog leash.
    style 946510 is wholly or mainly of nylon.
    % NY N291699: men's belt, outer layer of PU, middle of bonded leather
    % fibres, bottom of split cowhide: the leather girds the waist -> 4203.30
    the kind of style 75518C is belt.
    style 75518C is a composite good.
    the PU layer is a component of style 75518C.
    the cowhide layer is a component of style 75518C.
    the PU layer is wholly or mainly of polyurethane.
    the cowhide layer is wholly or mainly of split leather.
    the essential character of style 75518C is given by the cowhide layer,
        according to CBP, because "the leather girds the waist and thus constitutes the essential character of the belt".
    % articles the rulings above do not reach
    the kind of the leather jacket is jacket.
    the leather jacket is wholly or mainly of leather.
    the kind of the work gloves is gloves.
    the work gloves is wholly or mainly of leather.
    the kind of the batting gloves is gloves.
    the batting gloves is wholly or mainly of leather.
    the batting gloves is specially designed for use in sports.
    the coaster is a manufactured article.
    the coaster is wholly or mainly of leather.
    the string is a manufactured article.
    the string is wholly or mainly of gut.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the textile collar is 4201.00", "the subheading of style 946510 is 4201.00", "the subheading of style 75518C is 4203.30", "the subheading of the leather jacket is 4203.10", "the subheading of the work gloves is 4203.29", "the subheading of the batting gloves is 4203.21", "the subheading of the coaster is 4205.00", "the subheading of the string is 4206.00"].

% More of the rulings' containers and harness
scenario more_rulings is:
    % NY N291664: handbag with an outer surface of plastic sheeting -> 4202.22
    the kind of lot 174062 is handbag.
    the outer surface of lot 174062 is of sheeting of plastics.
    % NY N258431: wallet, outer surface 100 percent leather -> 4202.31
    the kind of style SL4266001 is wallet.
    the outer surface of style SL4266001 is of leather.
    % NY N248322: backpack, outer surface of man-made textile -> 4202.92
    the kind of the food backpack is backpack.
    the outer surface of the food backpack is of textile materials.
    % NY N334121: dog collars of metal chain -> 4201.00 (of any material)
    the kind of collar 50036 is dog collar.
    % HQ H285905: wrap phone case that also holds cards, exterior of
    % leather coated with polyurethane sheeting -> 4202.32
    the kind of the wrap case is phone wallet case.
    the outer surface of the wrap case is of sheeting of plastics.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of lot 174062 is 4202.22", "the subheading of style SL4266001 is 4202.31", "the subheading of the food backpack is 4202.92", "the subheading of collar 50036 is 4201.00", "the subheading of the wrap case is 4202.32"].

% The notes that send goods out of the chapter: a thin plastic carrier bag
% (note 3(A)(a), heading 3923) and a leather shoe (note 2(d), Chapter 64)
scenario exclusions is:
    the kind of the carrier bag is shopping bag.
    the carrier bag is a manufactured article.
    the carrier bag is made of plastics.
    the outer surface of the carrier bag is of sheeting of plastics.
    the carrier bag is not designed for prolonged use.
    the principal use of the carrier bag is packing of goods,
        according to CBP.
    the kind of the loafer is loafer.
    the loafer is a manufactured article.
    the loafer is wholly or mainly of leather.
    the constituent material of the upper of the loafer is leather.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of the loafer is leather.
    heading expects answers ["the heading of the carrier bag is 3923", "the heading of the loafer is 6403"].
